utils/fuzz-seam.py --accesses=addr-forms (completeness, not an oracle): one
NKI-shaped program rendered with its addresses in other forms (ptr.index
nodes, nested nodes, ptr.add chains, flat sums, commuted operands, split
constants, an index read through the copy of its tile, --lower-opt=false)
must give the same verdict and the same SeaM resolution counters
(Ackermann reads / constraints, open alias questions, A-INB state).
RUN: %python %sea_src_root/utils/fuzz-seam.py --sea-vc sea-vc %if !yices %{ --solver=z3 %} --seed 1 -n 8 --accesses=addr-forms | FileCheck %s
CHECK: programs: 8
CHECK: first-finding: none
CHECK: failures: 0

